{:exclude-files "(test/fixtures/|extensions/.*/target/|jolt/).*"
 ;; Reader views. kmet's .cljc files branch between its two hosts on the :bb
 ;; and :jolt reader features (plain code is what both run; :clj — the
 ;; JVM-ish dialect, matched by both hosts — is for code that must not run on
 ;; a non-JVM reader). This (project) config is the BABASHKA view:
 ;; `:cljc {:features [:clj]}` makes clj-kondo read the :clj branches, which is
 ;; what babashka reads; jolt/ and .jolt sources are bb-inert, hence excluded.
 ;; The JOLT view is
 ;; the other half: kmet.tasks.lint (tasks/kmet/tasks/lint.clj) projects the files whose
 ;; reading differs — those carrying :bb (into target/bb-lint/, under this
 ;; config) or :jolt (into target/jolt-lint/, under .clj-kondo-jolt/) — with
 ;; that feature token re-spelled :clj, the only feature clj-kondo matches.
 ;; The hosts' features are disjoint, so the rewrite reproduces each host's
 ;; selection exactly, wherever the branch sits.
 ;; NOTE: target/ must NOT be excluded here — the mirrors live under it and
 ;; kmet.tasks.lint passes them by path; it skips target/ itself when it walks a
 ;; directory. The overlay replaces this pattern (un-excluding jolt/, whose
 ;; provider-lib mirror is under target/jolt-lint/jolt/).
 :cljc {:features [:clj]}
 ;; test_http's deftest-transports/deftest-curl wrap clojure.test/deftest to
 ;; run each scenario under every HTTP transport mode — analyze them as
 ;; plain deftests so the defined test vars resolve.
 :lint-as {kmet.libs.test-http/deftest-transports clojure.test/deftest
           kmet.libs.test-http/deftest-curl clojure.test/deftest}
 ;; extensions/*.clj declare kmet.extensions.* namespaces that can never match
 ;; their extensions/... paths (clj-kondo derives the expected ns from the file
 ;; path), so the namespace-name-mismatch linter is off repo-wide; all other
 ;; linters still apply to extension code, which is part of `lint`.
 :linters {:namespace-name-mismatch {:level :off}}
 ;; kmet.app.extensions and its context machinery branch on the host at
 ;; their seams (loader-aware wraps a handler only on Jolt; track-cached-jar!
 ;; pins a jar only off Jolt; create-loader's params feed one branch each), so
 ;; each view sees the other branch's bindings go unused. The other view lints
 ;; it with the binding used, so an unused one is still caught there.
 :config-in-ns {kmet.app.extensions {:linters {:unused-binding {:level :off}}}
                kmet.app.extensions.context {:linters {:unused-binding {:level :off}}}}
 :hooks {:analyze-call {kmet.tui.macros/defcomponent hooks.kmet-macros/defcomponent
                        kmet.tui.macros/with-let     hooks.kmet-macros/with-let}}}
